meta {
  name: 02. Connect (Bearer Header - Ping)
  type: ws
  seq: 2
}

ws {
  url: {{wsBaseUrl}}/api/v1/ws
  body: ws
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:ws {
  name: ws.ping
  content: '''
    {
      "id": "ping-1",
      "event": "ws.ping"
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  # Connect WebSocket (Bearer Header)

  **Protocol:** `WebSocket` (`ws://` / `wss://`)
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/ws`
  **Auth:** `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` (Access Token)

  ## Description
  Opens an authenticated WebSocket connection using the `Authorization` header (recommended for non-browser clients, Bruno, Postman, and mobile apps).

  Upon connection, the server immediately emits `ws.connected` with your `conn_id` and `user_id`.
  Use the pre-configured message body to test sending an application-level `ws.ping` frame; the server replies with `ws.pong` carrying `"id": "ping-1"`.

  ## Prerequisite
  Run `Auth -> 05. Login (Identifier + Password)` first so `{{token}}` is populated in your environment.
}
